                <invention-title lang="de">STÜTZVORRICHTUNG FÜR MÖBELREGALE</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="fr">DISPOSITIF DE SUPPORT POUR ÉTAGÈRES DE MEUBLE</invention-title>
                <invention-title lang="en">SUPPORT DEVICE FOR FURNITURE SHELVES</invention-title>
            </bibliographic-data>
            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>The present invention relates to a supporting device (10, 10', 10", 10‴, 10ʺʺ, 10ʺ‴) for furniture shelves suitable for providing the reversible connection of a shelf (100) with the opposite shoulders (200) of a piece of furniture.According to the invention, the device (10, 10', 10'', 10''', 10ʺʺ, 10ʺ‴) comprises a main body (12) with which movable engagement means (15, 15', 15", 15‴) are slidingly associated, associated with a pin (11). The movable engagement means (15, 15', 15", 15‴) slide with respect to the main body (12) along a sliding direction (Y) between a first non-operating position in which said pin (11) does not protrude from said shelf (100), and a second operating position in which said pin (11) projects outwardly from a transverse edge (B) of said shelf (100).The supporting device (10) further comprises actuation means (13, 21, 32) of said engagement means (15, 15', 15", 15‴), and movement-transmission means (13b, 15c, 15b, 15c", 20, 21b, 31) suitable for transforming the movement of said actuation means (13, 21, 32) into a translational movement along the sliding direction (Y) of said movable engagement means (15, 15', 15", 15‴).</p>
            </abstract>
